  "term": "functional disorder",
  "definition": "Functional disorder is a broad label for a group of common conditions identified by particular patterns of bodily symptoms. Examples mentioned in the source include fibromyalgia, chronic fatigue syndrome, and irritable bowel syndrome, and these conditions can cause substantial physical limits and mental strain.",
